From ee2af7d54b79935964f9e613fa61a315a37990d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:03:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] ci(review-comment): answer PR #1382's review points
 (footer, writer race, Docker trigger)

PR #1382 (3dbd5428ff) made the ci-review-bot comment refresh when CI
completes on a wt/ head. Its exact-head review (card t_01a1cf7772b1ff84)
approved with three non-blocking points that merged unanswered:

1. Footer: the comment still said "refreshed hourly, not live" although
   it is now also refreshed on CI completion. It now reads "refreshed
   when CI or Docker completes on this head, and hourly; not live". The
   "<sub>ran on [sha](.../commits/<40hex>)" prefix that ship's BOT_HEAD
   parser reads is unchanged.

2. Writer race: the hourly sweep (one run, many PRs, one shared
   concurrency group) and a targeted workflow_run refresh (a per-head
   group) can both hold a snapshot of the same PR. A sweep that started
   at :17 but reached the PR after a targeted run overwrote the newer
   snapshot with its older one until the next sweep. Each write now puts
   a hidden state line right after the marker:
     <!-- hermes-ci-review-bot:state head=<40hex> started=<UTC us> run=<id> -->
   Right before writing (after the existing head/open re-read), the run
   reads the bot comment; if it holds a snapshot of the same head from a
   run that started at or after this one, it skips and logs why. Another
   head, or a comment without a state line (written before this change),
   is replaced as before. A per-head concurrency group can't do this,
   because one sweep run covers every PR.

3. Docker trigger: the comment reports "Docker Build, Test, and Publish"
   (WATCH_WORKFLOWS), but only CI triggered a refresh. When Docker
   finishes after CI (a rerun, a slow build), the comment showed it
   pending until the next sweep. Docker now triggers too, by its exact
   name: and with the same wt/** filter. TRIGGER_WORKFLOW (the
   workflow_run's name, compared for equality only) lets a Docker
   completion while that head's CI is still running write nothing and
   spend no collection calls, since CI's own completion refreshes.

Proof: tests/ci/test_batch_review_comments.py goes from 34 to 48
collected cases (none removed). 17 fail with the 3dbd5428ff script and
workflow (footer, same-head ordering incl. the equal-start tie, state
written after the marker with the compared comment id, Docker in the
trigger list by exact name, sibling-before-CI skip, env wiring) and all
pass here. 17 source mutants (each new condition flipped or dropped)
are all killed. 93 tests in the batch/live-comment/runner-routing files
pass; actionlint 1.7.12 (the pinned version) clean on every workflow.
